        "Text": {
          "type": "cexolocstring",
          "value": {
            "0": "*What you took for a tree is not a tree. Bark cracks like an old door, and two green lights open in the knot of its face.* Hoom... hom. Twelve of us still walk in Fangorn. I am the thirteenth, and I have been standing a very long while. Root-sleep is warm, little druid, and I have nearly forgotten my own name.\n\nHoo -- but there is one taste that wakes me. The truffles of the deep loam. They hide from eyes and from hands; only a boar's nose has ever found one. Bring me a truffle with the earth-smell still on it, and set the Balance of green things about my roots, and I will remember who I am."
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "__struct_id": 2,
        "Animation": {
          "type": "dword",
          "value": 0
