        },
        "Text": {
          "type": "cexolocstring",
          "value": {
            "0": "*Two green lights open slowly in the bark.* Hoom... a singer. It has been an age of the world since anything sang in this wood that was not the wind.\n\nI am the thirteenth Ent of Fangorn, and I have stood so long that my own name has gone down into my roots after the water. Play me awake, singer. Twice: once to bring me up out of the root-sleep, and once more to bring me back my name. But do not hurry me -- nothing good is ever said in a hurry -- and do not play falsely. If you do, I will go down again, and I will not come up for a day and a night."
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "__struct_id": 3,
        "Animation": {
          "type": "dword",
          "value": 0
        },
        "AnimLoop": {
          "type": "byte",
          "value": 1
