          "value": ""
        },
        "Text": {
          "type": "cexolocstring",
          "value": {
            "0": "*Leaflock's voice slows to a creak.* Wear the boar, then. Go on four feet among my roots and snuff the loam -- what is hidden will show itself to a snout and to nothing else in the world.\n\nAnd do not dawdle. A truffle out of the earth dies quickly, and a dead truffle wakes nobody. Come back to me with it, put off the beast-shape, and sing the Balance of Nature over my roots -- close, mind. My hearing is all in my bark."
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "__struct_id": 6,
        "Animation": {
          "type": "dword",
          "value": 0
        },
        "AnimLoop": {
          "type": "byte",
